       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Requested:** metformin 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as up to 850 mg three times daily. Single doses above 1,000 mg are not typical.\n- **Risk:** This is twice the maximum daily dose. It raises the risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided into doses\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to review it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
